## Passage-retrieval probe (DenseOn / LateOn)

- Dense/late-interaction models are **answer-engine retrieval probes**, not Google ranking factors.
- Local entry: `raw-sources/tools/pylate` + `fast-plaid`. HF DenseOn/LateOn weights stay **Watch** (~600MB+; over default adopt cap) until operator pulls outside wiki disk budget.
- Prefer late-interaction for long service pages; never pull multi-GB embedding datasets into this laptop.
- Layout/tabular caveat (K154 READ steal): dense top-k can separate figures from unit/fiscal headers — dense/late probes stay for **prose** service pages; do not claim dense RAG solves table-heavy PDFs. No READ local clone (code Watch).

## Easy Review + hands-on policy

- Draft review replies in-wiki / Easy Review; **operator posts**. Never automate review gating or selective solicitation.
- Never bulk-identical GBP posts; coordinate NAP edits with citations; schema must match reality.

## K254 — GBP "Edited" review indicator (2026-09-02)

**Brief:** `briefs/2026-09-02_k254-seo-gbp-edited-review.md`
**Concept:** `@seo-wiki/concepts/google-review-edited-indicator.md`
**Source:** `@osint-wiki/sources/newsletter-rss-sterling-sky-2026-08-30-what-does-it-mean-when-a-google-review-shows-edi.md`

- When Google shows **Edited** on a review, the reviewer changed text after posting — **not** fraud by default.
- Monitor sentiment shifts; document owner responses in Easy Review — **operator posts** (never automate review gating).
- Do not bulk-flag edited reviews as spam without case-by-case read.
- `wire_status: policy_wired` on concept page.

